## Original Content
Chinese President Xi Jinping held talks with visiting King of the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing on Monday afternoon.

## Summary
Chinese President Xi Jinping met with King Abdullah II of Jordan in Beijing to discuss deepening the alignment of their development strategies. The talks were held at the Great Hall of the People on Monday afternoon.

## Key Points
- Xi Jinping and King Abdullah II held diplomatic talks in Beijing.
- The discussion focused on aligning development strategies between China and Jordan.
- The meeting took place at the Great Hall of the People, indicating high-level engagement.


